                <p> Kapa=CA=BBa Bypass Green Waste Site Now Open; Green Was=
te Closed at Kapa=CA=BBa Transfer Station<br><br>The County of Kaua=CA=BBi =
Department of Public Works Solid Waste Division has opened the temporary gr=
een waste site off Kapa=CA=BBa Bypass Road. Residents in the Kapa=CA=BBa ar=
ea should bring green waste to this site, which will close at 3:30 p.m. tod=
ay. The site will open again tomorrow from 7:15 a.m. to 3:30 p.m.<br><br>Wi=
th the Bypass site open, the Kapa=CA=BBa Refuse Transfer Station is no long=
er accepting green waste. The transfer station remains open for trash.<br><=
br>Other facilities:<br><br>    =E2=80=A2    Hanap=C4=93p=C4=93 Refuse Tran=
sfer Station and Kekaha Landfill are open for trash and green waste.<br><br=
>    =E2=80=A2    L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe Refuse Transfer Station is accepting tra=
sh only.<br><br>    =E2=80=A2    Hanalei Refuse Transfer Station is open fo=
r mixed waste only. No green waste, metals, or appliances can be accepted a=
t this time.<br><br>Refuse collection:<br><br>    =E2=80=A2    Crews are co=
llecting trash today at limited capacity in L=C4=81wa=CA=BBi, Kal=C4=81heo,=
 and =CA=BB=C5=8Cma=CA=BBo.<br><br>    =E2=80=A2    Regular islandwide coll=
ection for Monday customers should resume Monday, Sept. 14, in accessible a=
reas.<br><br>HI-5 redemption in L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe has restarted. All other l=
ocations remain closed until equipment is repaired.
<br>Message Sender: Mystiana Victorino  =20
<br>Notification Status: New   </p>
